{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's sensor and actuator interface, separating perception and motion. The specification encodes a safe, coverage-oriented exploration policy: random_walk is used in clear states for exploration, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, directed recovery turns. Recovery states only allow a single turn action and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is only enabled in a dedicated search state after repeated blockages. All transitions are deterministic and safe.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception (sensors) and motion (actuators) to reflect real robot architecture.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-oriented exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, directed turns for obstacle recovery, and minimal use of full_rotate."
  ],
